+### 1.7 A group image with no start letter — `patches/fixes/0005-group-image-with-no-start-letter.patch`
+
+Also in the second patch group, and again a send to `#f`. A group is born with the start letter of its
+first object, `(tell (1st ordered-objects) 'get-descriptor-for plato-letter-category)` (`groups.ss:81-82`), and
+`make-image` is given that as the image's start letter (`groups.ss:90`). When the group's first object is itself a
+length-based group, that object has no letter category (fix 0001 already lets such a group have none,
+`groups.ss:43-47`), so the new group's image has the start letter `#f`. This is common and harmless:
+`relationship-between`, `shorten`, `extend`, `enumerate-letter`, `reverse-medium` and the letter branch of
+`new-start-letter` all treat an absent letter by failing or by staying absent. Two sites did not:
+
+- **`new-start-letter`, group branch** (`images.ss:281`): `(set! start-letter (tell start-letter 'get-related-node arg))`
+  with a platonic relation (successor, predecessor, identity) sent `get-related-node` to `#f`. `answer-finder`
+  reaches it through `apply-transforms`, `transform-image` and the image's `new-start-letter`
+  (`wxyz -> xxyz; fgzzz`, seed 27, at codelet 2851: `Exception: attempt to apply non-procedure #f`). In all 41
+  runs found, the image was a length-based group of two objects whose first object is itself a length-based
+  group (`xy` + `aaa`, `fg` + `zzz`), and the sub-images had already done their work on the line before.
+- **`new-start-letter`, letter-image branch** (`images.ss:274`): the same send for a letter image whose start
+  letter is `#f`. No recorded run reaches it (a letter image always has its letter); a directed trial does.
+
+The patch is written on the two lines it replaces:
+
+- **`images.ss:274`** is `(let ((new-letter (and (exists? start-letter) (tell start-letter 'get-related-node arg)))) ...`:
+  no start letter has no related letter, so the branch fails, as it already does when the related letter does not exist.
+- **`images.ss:281`** is `(set! start-letter (and (exists? start-letter) (tell start-letter 'get-related-node arg)))`:
+  none stays none (the sub-images have already been given the relation).
+
+**Effect on behaviour: none where it does not fire.** An image with a start letter takes the same branch as before,
+and every image that reaches the new code ended the run in an error. Rejected: giving the image a start letter at birth
+(it changes runs that do not crash and undoes fix 0001's withholding), taking the letter from the first sub-image,
+calling `(fail)` in the group branch (completed rule applications would snag), and catching the error in `answer-finder`.
+
